{"content":[{"c":["ABIHU"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Second son of Aaron and Elisheba (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.6.23","r":"Exod.6.23","rawR":"Exod.6.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.6.23","value":"Exod.6.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 6:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.60","r":"Num.26.60","rawR":"Num.26.60","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.60","value":"Num.26.60"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:60"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.3","r":"1Chr.6.3","rawR":"1Chr.6.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.3","value":"1Chr.6.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:3"},"). Abihu and his brother Nadab joined Moses, Aaron, and the 70 elders of Israel in worshiping the glory of God on Mt Sinai (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.24.1-11","r":"Exod.24.1-11","rawR":"Exod.24.1-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.24.1-11","value":"Exod.24.1-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 24:1-11"},"). The four sons of Aaron were made priests along with their father (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.28.1","r":"Exod.28.1","rawR":"Exod.28.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.28.1","value":"Exod.28.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 28:1"},"), but later Abihu and Nadab were burned to death for offering “a different kind of fire” before the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.10.1","r":"Lev.10.1","rawR":"Lev.10.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.10.1","value":"Lev.10.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 10:1"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"; see also ",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.2-4","r":"Num.3.2-4","rawR":"Num.3.2-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.2-4","value":"Num.3.2-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 3:2-4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.61","r":"Num.26.61","rawR":"Num.26.61","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.61","value":"Num.26.61"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:61"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.1-2","r":"1Chr.24.1-2","rawR":"1Chr.24.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.1-2","value":"1Chr.24.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24:1-2"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Abihu","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationRefer